-- title:
--   One-dimensional dual-number tangent space bounds the relative cotangent space
-- statement:
--   Let $\Lambda$ be a commutative local ring and let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring equipped with a $\Lambda$-algebra structure, and assume that the composite of $\operatorname{algebraMap} \Lambda R$ with the residue map $R \to k_R := \mathrm{ResidueField}\,R$ is surjective, so that every residue class of $R$ is hit by $\Lambda$. Let $\Phi_1 : R \to k_R[\varepsilon]$ be a $\Lambda$-algebra homomorphism into the dual numbers over $k_R$ whose first component is the residue map, i.e. $(\Phi_1 r)_{\mathrm{fst}} = \mathrm{residue}\,R\,r$ for all $r \in R$, and assume that $\Phi_1$ spans all such maps in the following sense: for every $\Lambda$-algebra homomorphism $\Phi : R \to k_R[\varepsilon]$ with $(\Phi r)_{\mathrm{fst}} = \mathrm{residue}\,R\,r$ for all $r$, there is a scalar $c \in k_R$ with $(\Phi r)_{\mathrm{snd}} = c \,(\Phi_1 r)_{\mathrm{snd}}$ for all $r \in R$. Then there exists an element $t$ of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$ of $R$ such that $$\mathfrak m_R \subseteq (t) + \mathfrak m_R^2 + \mathfrak m_\Lambda R,$$ where $(t)$ is the ideal generated by $t$ and $\mathfrak m_\Lambda R$ denotes the image of the maximal ideal of $\Lambda$ under $\operatorname{algebraMap} \Lambda R$.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the classical criterion relating the tangent space of a deformation functor, computed by $\Lambda$-algebra maps to dual numbers lying over the residue map, to the relative cotangent space $\mathfrak m_R/(\mathfrak m_R^2 + \mathfrak m_\Lambda R)$: a tangent space of dimension at most one forces the relative cotangent space to be generated by a single element. It is used in the identification of certain Hecke or deformation rings with quotients of a one-variable power series ring over $\Lambda$, via the finiteness-and-regularity step invoked in the modular-curve level packages.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_maximalIdeal_le_span_sup_sq_sup_map_of_forall_algHom_dualNumber.lean

